LINUX CHEATSHEET
Quick reference: commands, types, variables & fundamentals
Share / copy freely

=== FUNDAMENTALS ===
Everything is a file (regular, dir, symlink, device, pipe, socket)
Paths:  /absolute   ./relative   ../parent   ~/home
Variables:
  NAME=value          # set
  echo $NAME          # expand
  export PATH=$PATH:/opt/bin
Special vars:
  $0 script name   $1 $2 args   $# arg count
  $? last exit code (0=ok)   $$ current PID   $USER $HOME $PATH $PWD
Permissions (rwx rwx rwx = owner group others):
  r=4  w=2  x=1     755 = rwxr-xr-x    644 = rw-r--r--
  chmod 755 file    chmod +x script    chown user:group file
Redirection & pipes:
  cmd > file        overwrite
  cmd >> file       append
  cmd 2> err.log    stderr
  cmd 2>&1          both to stdout
  cmd | other       pipe
Wildcards: * any string   ? one char   [abc] set   {a,b} brace
Quoting: 'literal'   "expand $vars"   $(cmd) or `cmd`
File types (file command / ls -l first char):
  - regular   d directory   l symlink   b block   c char   p pipe   s socket

